### Day 16: AI-assisted refactor verification
### Purpose: prove behaviour is unchanged after refactoring.
### Run Spring Boot first: mvn spring-boot:run

### Login as seeded admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}


### Copy token from login response
@token = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE


### Get protected asset list - should still work
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create asset - should still work
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/assets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetTag": "REFAC-2026-001",
  "name": "Refactor Test Asset",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-REFAC-001",
  "location": "Training Lab"
}


### Duplicate create - should still return 409 Conflict
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/assets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetTag": "REFAC-2026-001",
  "name": "Duplicate Refactor Test Asset",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-REFAC-002",
  "location": "Training Lab"
}


### Update asset - replace id with an existing asset id
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/assets/PASTE_EXISTING_ASSET_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetTag": "REFAC-2026-001",
  "name": "Refactor Test Asset Updated",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-REFAC-001",
  "status": "ASSIGNED",
  "location": "Training Lab",
  "assignedTo": "trainer@example.com"
}


### Invalid status - should still return 400 Bad Request
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/assets/PASTE_EXISTING_ASSET_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "assetTag": "REFAC-2026-001",
  "name": "Refactor Test Asset Updated",
  "category": "Camera",
  "serialNumber": "SN-REFAC-001",
  "status": "BROKEN",
  "location": "Training Lab",
  "assignedTo": "trainer@example.com"
}
